# Deny by default: COPY . . in the Dockerfile copies only what is let back
# in below, so nothing kept out of git (the evaluation's export of the live
# database, local notes and review reports, tools' settings, secrets) can
# reach an image, whatever its name. tests/unit/test_dockerfile.py checks
# both what stays out and what the build needs.
*

# What the image needs: the package's build files (pyproject.toml names
# README.md and LICENSE), its source, the dashboard's theme and the
# committed lists.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!requirements.txt
!src/
!config/
!.streamlit/config.toml

# Still out, inside what is let back in. Docker matches a pattern from the
# context's root only, unlike .gitignore, so these start with **/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
